        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0569" n="1303" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1303"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 607.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 614, of the 4th
                    instant, concerning the case of Mardiros K. Mooradian.</p>
                <p>As your telegrams of September 9 and 12 report Mooradian’s release and “joyful”
                    departure, it is presumed the incident is closed.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
